Package: erhai-sensors
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: @DEPENDS@, iio-sensor-proxy, systemd, udev
Conflicts: hexagonrpcd
Description: OnePlus Pad 2 Pro rotation and ambient light sensors
 Connects the Qualcomm Sensor Core on the ADSP to the desktop: a private
 hexagonrpcd file server attaches the ADSP sensor domain and serves it the
 stock sensor configuration, libssc reads motion and light over QRTR, and a
 private iio-sensor-proxy build with SSC support replaces the distribution
 binary through a systemd drop-in. Distribution files are left unchanged;
 removing the package restores Ubuntu's iio-sensor-proxy at the next boot.
 .
 The per-unit sensor registry is not included. Import it once with
 erhai-sensors-import-registry from a copy of this tablet's Android persist
 data; until then the stack stays inactive. The accelerometer startup gate checks
 real gravity samples. Ambient light uses independent upstream discovery.
 Light integration is a development candidate awaiting hardware acceptance;
 the accelerometer mount matrix still needs the four-orientation test.
 .
 The accelerometer stream is requested with non-wakeup delivery and without
 batching, so the sensor core does not interrupt the processor for every
 sample; sensors that exist to wake the system keep wake-up delivery. For
 measurements or as a fallback, erhai-sensors-ssc-delivery overrides the
 delivery or adds batching for the current boot only ("wakeup" restores the
 requests of upstream libssc).
 .
 Across system sleep the sensor streams are paused: erhai-sensors-sleep
 stops iio-sensor-proxy on the way into sleep, which closes its streams,
 and starts it again after wake-up, when its clients claim the sensors
 anew. Otherwise the sensor core would keep sending samples, and each
 message ends a deep suspend. "systemctl disable erhai-sensors-sleep"
 turns this off.
